    <!-- ═══ 08 · WORKING WITH YOUR TEAM ═══ -->
    <section id="working-together" class="cgo-dark relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" style="background: radial-gradient(120% 90% at 50% 0%, hsl(42 40% 30% / 0.1), transparent 55%);"></div>
      <div class="relative container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 max-w-4xl cgo-reveal">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-gold-gradient text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[44px] leading-tight mb-10">Working with your team</h2>

        <div class="font-body text-lg leading-relaxed space-y-7 max-w-[65ch]">
          <p>The programme is not delivered as a fixed package dropped into every setting. Before the group begins, I meet with the relevant staff member or team to understand the population, the current programme, the risks, the language, the culture, and what your organisation actually hopes the group will add.</p>

          <p class="cgo-emph">The first step is understanding who will be sitting in the room.</p>

          <p>Where possible, a staff member or social worker who already knows the participants is welcome to join the group. This is encouraged rather than required. Familiar staff involvement helps participants enter the group with more trust, and strengthens the continuity between what happens in the room and the support your organisation provides the rest of the week.</p>

          <p>An initial hand-off into the first session is strongly encouraged in every setting. A group that begins with someone the participants already trust in the room tends to settle considerably faster than one that begins with a stranger.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mt-12 pt-10 border-t border-parchment/15">
          <div>
            <p class="cgo-gold-light-text font-body text-xs tracking-[0.14em] uppercase mb-3">Before</p>
