            <p class="font-heading text-xl text-parchment/90 mb-1">Michael Kaplan</p>
            <p class="font-body text-sm cgo-gold-light-text tracking-wide leading-relaxed mb-7">ASCHP-registered Wellness Counsellor (Reg. 10559) &middot; Group facilitator &middot; Founder of Sangham</p>
            <div class="font-body text-lg leading-relaxed space-y-6 max-w-[62ch]">
              <p>Michael has more than a decade of experience working with boys and young men through mentoring, group facilitation and counselling, including many years within the Boys to Men community in Cape Town.</p>
              <p>His work combines relational counselling, group process, and long experience with mindfulness and contemplative practice. Much of that development took place under the guidance of clinical psychologist Bernard Altman, particularly around adolescent developmental work and group process.</p>
              <p class="cgo-emph">A particular focus of the work is translating psychological and contemplative ideas into experiences people can actually use, without requiring academic language or previous meditation experience.</p>
              <p>The emphasis is on meeting people where they are, taking their ways of coping seriously, and helping them develop greater awareness and choice.</p>
